\\ The remote effect Ledger, as every member of the ledger system declares it.
\\
\\ This file holds declarations only. The caller's program (ledger-caller.fen)
\\ and the peer's program (ledger-peer.fen) both include it, so neither can
\\ state the effect differently from the other: (include "ledger.decl.fen").
\\ Each image carries a digest of this signature, read-only markers included,
\\ and the supervisor assembles the system only if the caller's digest is the
\\ serving peer's (EFFECTS.md §12.6).
\\
\\   add    changes the peer's state. A caller performs it with a request key
\\          first, (perform Ledger add key amount); the peer applies a key once.
\\          Its result is (status, value): status 0 is ok with the value, the
\\          total after the addition; status 1 is conflict, the key having been
\\          applied with another argument.
\\   total  is read-only: no key, nothing recorded, nothing changed.

(remote-effect Ledger
  (add I64 --> (Tuple I64 I64))
  (read-only total Unit --> I64))
